name: sim.addGraphCurve
description: Adds or updates a graph curve. A graph curve is persistent, but can be removed with sim.destroyGraphCurve
luaSynopsis: int curveId = sim.addGraphCurve(int graphHandle, string curveName, int dim, list streamIds, list defaultValues, string unitStr, int options = 0, list color = [0 1, 0], int curveWidth = 2)
pythonSynopsis: int curveId = sim.addGraphCurve(int graphHandle, string curveName, int dim, int[] streamIds, float[] defaultValues, string unitStr, int options = 0, float[3] color = {0, 1, 0}, int curveWidth = 2)
inputs:
1. graphHandle: handle of the graph
2. curveName: name of the curve
3. dim: dimension of the curve. Valid values are 2 or 3
4. streamIds: array of 2 or 3 graph streams (x/y curves require 2 stream IDs, xyz curves require 3 stream IDs). Indicate -1 for a missing stream, in which case a default value will be used instead
5. defaultValues: array of 2 or 3 default values
6. unitStr: string describing the unit of the curve. Can be None/nil
7. options: bit-coded:
    - bit0 is not used.
    - If bit1 is set (2), the label is not visible
    - If bit2 is set (4), the points are not linked
8. color: rgb-triplet, with values between 0.0 and 1.0, indicating the color of the stream. Can be None/nil
9. curveWidth: the width of an xyz curve
outputs:
1. curveId: id of the created/updated curve
replacedBy:
- name: addCurve, class: graph, file: graph_addCurve.method
